  "summary": "LibreOffice Impress is a free, open-source presentation software equivalent to Microsoft Office PowerPoint, compatible with Windows and GNU/Linux operating systems. When installing via package management, the complete option should be selected. Impress can be launched through the Applications menu under Office, either directly or via the main LibreOffice startup dialog by choosing the presentation component. The Impress interface includes title, menu, standard, formatting, and status toolbars. Users can create a presentation from a template by selecting an option such as Recommendation of a Strategy, choosing slide designs like Presentation Backgrounds with a Blue Border, setting the output medium to Original, and specifying presenter details and presentation subjects. The default headings provided in the wizard can be retained to generate the slides. Finally, presentations are saved by selecting File and Save, which defaults to the Open Document Format with the .odp file extension, and can be reopened later from the File menu.",
